Pages = {385-403},
Month = {SUM},
Abstract = {Although past researchers have sometimes labeled American Indians
   ``hard-to-reach,{''} a review of the literature identifies several
   available strategies for improving sampling and response rates for
   surveys of this population. After discussing various approaches to
   defining who is American Indian, this article summarizes the literature
   on challenges in conducting research in American Indian populations. The
   literature strongly points to the need for full and active partnerships
   between American Indian communities and outside researchers in order to
   ensure that the communities are respected, protected, and benefit from
   the research. Full and active partnerships also are needed to improve
   the quality of data collected in American Indian communities. Successful
   strategies used in U.S. Census Bureau enumeration efforts exemplify the
   recommendations for participatory research with American Indian
   communities.},
